{"actor_ref":"claude","class":"draft_history","document_uuid":"01a1a54a-317b-738e-8f02-4c6becac2718","id":"01a1a5d4-31a5-74d4-961f-ed9437d5288f","idempotency_key":"16caab12964f4df235569a51e91e42fd851e44cf891748ca28d1c2452d720ebe","occurred_at":"2026-11-04T09:11:49Z","payload":{"note":"crates/ai/src/play.rs plus routes. PlayPolicy is the gate: casual allows chat, hints, engine use and takebacks; competitive allows none of them and does not even ask the model for reasoning (request_reasoning false), so nothing depends on the model choosing to stay quiet. request_move asks for exactly one SAN/UCI move, validates it with Match::apply against the real position, feeds a refusal back with the reason and retries up to MatchConfig::max_retries, leaving the board untouched when the budget runs out. Match::takeback rebuilds the position from the move list rather than reversing it, so a half-applied move cannot survive, and refuses once the match is finished. Server: POST /api/ai/matches/{id}/model-move, /takeback and /chat; a rated match is treated as competitive, an unrated one as casual. Evidence: cargo test -p rbc-ai --all-features play -> 13 tests (policy flags and refusals, move requested and recorded with the prompt naming side/FEN/legal moves/format, illegal reply retried with the reason, retry budget respected without touching the board, reasoning hidden in competitive, chat refused before the model is asked, chat answered in casual, takeback restores the start position and refuses a finished match, model seat lookup, prompt shape). Live: casual e4 -> model e5 (1 attempt), chat answered, takeback removed e5; rated refused chat and takeback and hid reasoning. Browser: cdp_ai_play.js -> AI_PLAY_PASS.","target":"t-bf5d"},"type":"work.note_added","v":2}
